# Brewlette

Beer roulette for an iPad behind a bar. Fun bar toy — not enterprise software.

Follow [`.cursorrules`](../.cursorrules) for visual system (“Taproom Roulette”). Summarized below.

## Stack (do not change without asking)

- React + Vite + JavaScript
- HTML Canvas wheel; CSS design tokens in `src/styles/`
- `localStorage` via `src/utils/storage.js` only
- Static site only — **no** backend, auth, API, DB, Firebase, Next.js

## Architecture

Prefer: `components/`, `hooks/useBeerList.js`, `utils/{storage,random,wheel}.js`, `data/defaultBeers.js`.

Wheel math in `wheel.js`; crypto selection in `random.js`. **Pick winner first, then animate.**

## Design — Taproom Roulette

- **Fonts:** Poller One (brand), Abril Fatface (headers/results), Arvo (UI/body)
- **Headers:** uppercase + wide tracking
- **Palette:** near-black dive (`#0B0D11` / `#12161A`), marquee cream (`#FDFBF7`), lager gold, Schlitz red, dive green — no pastels / purple SaaS
- **Polaroid cards** for results/editor items: cream face, dark ink, thick bottom padding, hard zero-blur shadows
- **Chunky borders** (`3px`), sharp corners — not hairline soft UI
- **Wheel:** mechanical carnival feel; easing `cubic-bezier(0.12, 1, 0.33, 1)` / `easeMechanical`
- Reject Inter/Roboto, purple gradients, neon glow spam

## UX invariants

- Wheel-first Spin Mode; subtle Edit entry
- Touch targets ≥ 44px (prefer 48px); hover never required
- `prefers-reduced-motion`: shorter spin, still show result
- Empty / 1-beer / corrupt storage / long names must not break
- Optional “Remove this beer” after spin — never auto-remove

